<title>LITHUANIA: BOURSE CAPITALISATION ROSE TO 5.381 BLN.</title>
<headline>BOURSE CAPITALISATION ROSE TO 5.381 BLN.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The capitalisation of the Vilnius</p>
<p>bourse rose to 5.381 billion litas last week from 5.380 billion</p>
<p>litas the previous week, the stock exchange said on Monday.</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse statistics:</p>
<p>					 June 14-18	 June 07-11</p>
<p>    Submitted orders	     15,495		14,296</p>
<p>    Executed orders		909		   945</p>
<p>Number of transactions on</p>
<p>    Central market (CM)	  717		   711</p>
<p>    Turnover on the CM in LTL  25,140,950	  2,840,120</p>
<p>Number of transactions in</p>
<p>    block trades (BT)	    97		    116</p>
<p>    Turnover of BT in LTL	25,887,780	  11,323,770</p>
<p>    Supply of shares per week  52,884,599	  47,292,878</p>
<p>    Demand of shares per week  8,076,976	   6,081,934</p>
<p>Turnover of shares</p>
<p>    on CM per week in LTL	3,565,900	   2,454,740</p>
<p>    in BT per week in LTL	25,887,780	  11,323,770</p>
<p>The number of transactions</p>
<p>    in government T-bills	20		    6</p>
<p>The turnover of government</p>
<p>    T-bills in LTL per week    21,575,040	  385,380</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
